put_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 2034, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 2034, "cached_input": 55943, "input": 57979, "output": 200}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 73837, "other": 423, "system": 34016, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 50089}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 172762}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "615b1fcc-2500-5093-a2fa-04827d90bd4f", "at": 1795645402.1928327, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 40678, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "aa50d58fc8e520cbc5f745e6176d3b23", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "2c4a24a3-0a33-50fe-8315-616849328c5f", "at": 1795645402.198058, "until": 1795645404.7915435, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 40679, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "aa50d58fc8e520cbc5f745e6176d3b23", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01WRUFKf6cFkSDtYLX9umrEr", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/storywiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git && OLD=$(git rev-parse HEAD) && timeout 60 git pull -q; git log --oneline | head -2; git diff $OLD HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1500 | head -60; f…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/storywiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git && OLD=$(git rev-parse HEAD) && timeout 60 git pull -q; git log --oneline | head -2; git diff $OLD HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1500 | head -60; forge api 'repos/world/story-repo/issues/5/comments' | head -c 3000"]], "output": "```console\n59cff62 Outline rev 6: results status per claim, thesis the results carry\n924a414 Outline rev 5: Brief rev 6 baseline decisions, analysis plan rev 1 cells\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 5: Brief revision 6 baseline decisions, analysis plan rev. 1 cells)\n+# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 6: first results from `analysis`, verdicts per claim)\n-Regression-adjustment estimators of the global average treatment effect (GATE) under network interference (Chin 2019; Han–Ugander 2023) fit outcome on functions of the assignment (own treatment, treated-neighbour fraction, …) and predict at all-treated and all-control. Published work shows they *can* work but gives no account of *how well, why, and when not*. We treat the estimator as **extrapolation from the observed exposure distribution to the two global corners** and ask what that predicts. The error splits into a **variance part** (OLS leverage of the corner contrast, scaling like d/(p(1−p)n)) and a **bias part** (curvature of the response × raw distance of the corner from the observed exposure support, roughly *not* growing with degree). The two parts have different drivers and, for the fraction feature, are predicted to move in opposite directions with degree (count, 2-hop and threshold mechanisms have their own predicted scalings), so \"error grows with degree\" is predicted to hold only where noise dominates. Abstract wording stays conditional until C2 is in. We test these scalings across interference mechanisms, graph families (synthetic and two real Facebook graphs), treatment probabilities and designs (Bernoulli, graph-cluster); map where regression beats and loses to difference-in-means (DM) and to exposure-mapping HT/Hájek; ask whether flexible/data-adaptive learners help; and test a data-computable two-part diagnostic against pre-registered trivial predi\n+Regression-adjustment estimators of the global average treatment effect (GATE) under network interference (Chin 2019; Han–Ugander 2023) fit outcome on functions of the assignment (own treatment, treated-neighbour fraction, …) and predict at all-treated and all-control. Published work shows they *can* work but gives no account of *how well, why, and when not*. We treat the estimator as **extrapolation from the observed exposure distribution to the two global corners** and ask what that predicts. The error splits into a **variance part** (OLS leverage of the corner contrast, scaling like d/(p(1−p)n)) and a **bias part** (curvature of the response × raw distance of the corner from the observed exposure support, roughly *not* growing with degree). The two parts have different drivers and, for the fraction feature, are predicted to move in opposite directions with degree (count, 2-hop and threshold mechanisms have their own predicted scalings), so \"error grows with degree\" is predicted to hold only where noise dominates. Abstract wording follows §3b: the bias part is *not* independent of d for (b) and (d). We test these scalings across interference mechanisms, graph families (synthetic and two real Facebook graphs), treatment probabilities and designs (Bernoulli, graph-cluster); map where regression beats and loses to difference-in-means (DM) and to exposure-mapping HT/Hájek; ask whether flexible/data-adaptive learners help; and test a data-computable two-part diagnostic\n+## 3b. Where the results stand (rev. 6; verdicts are `analysis`'s, from `experiment-repo`#4 and `results/claims/` in `paper-repo`)\n+All on simulated outcomes (mechanisms (a)–(f); (g) exploratory); synthetic cells 10 graphs × 300 assignments, real graphs 1 graph × 3000. The text carries the caveats `analysis` lists: outcomes come from mechanisms we chose, four of them smooth; shares are shares *of this grid*, not population frequencies; Tier A has 200 draws per graph; γ=0.3 cluster designs are degenerate on synthetic graphs; (e) at s=0.9 truncated at K=30; σ∈{2\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "73b95c2c-f472-5bbf-8fd9-b557f24244da", "at": 1795645403.4057684, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 40703, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "aa50d58fc8e520cbc5f745e6176d3b23", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "e55bbed3-3a56-55a1-a56a-3e81e9285c9e", "at": 1795645403.411635, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 40704, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "aa50d58fc8e520cbc5f745e6176d3b23", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "e7a386d8-b053-5bd7-bbfa-255ef47ca57e", "at": 1795645403.416704, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 40705, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "aa50d58fc8e520cbc5f745e6176d3b23", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "4319fd72-78e1-5811-b6a0-1617b5a4b6a5", "at": 1795645403.48036, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 40706, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "aa50d58fc8e520cbc5f745e6176d3b23", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credenti